## Intuition
Use backtracking to explore every valid path from the top-left cell to the bottom-right cell. At each cell, try moving in all four directions while avoiding blocked cells, out-of-bounds positions, and cells already used in the current path. When the destination is reached, store the sequence of moves.

## Approach
- Return an empty list if the grid is empty or the starting cell is blocked.
- Maintain a visited_grid to prevent revisiting cells in the current path.
- Recursively try moves in the order U, R, D, and L.
- A move is valid only if it stays inside the grid, lands on a cell containing 1, and has not been visited.
- Mark a cell as visited before recursion, then unmark it afterward to backtrack.
- On reaching (n-1, n-1), append the constructed path string to ans.

